<BaseLayout current="About" title="About">
  <div class="eyebrow">ABOUT</div><h1>A curious mind, an engineering perspective.</h1>
  <div class="prose">
    <p class="lede">I am Koami Moïse Agbenowossi. My interests sit at the intersection of science, engineering, technology and the development of industrial capabilities.</p>
    <p>I am drawn to the work of understanding complex subjects: reading deeply, following an argument, questioning assumptions and connecting ideas across disciplines. I am especially interested in how scientific knowledge becomes engineering methods, products and systems.</p>
    <h2>Areas I keep returning to</h2>
    <ul><li>Mechanical and mechatronic engineering</li><li>Advanced manufacturing and materials science</li><li>Robotics, control and intelligent systems</li><li>Research methods, design and optimization</li><li>Industrial development and technological capability</li></ul>
    <h2>Why this website exists</h2>
    <p>This website is a public record of my learning. It gives me a place to explain what I think I understand, expose gaps in my reasoning, keep track of questions and share work that may be useful to others.</p>
    <h2>A long-term ambition</h2>
    <p>I would like to contribute to building a robotics and innovation laboratory in Togo: a place where people can study scientific ideas, design mechanical systems, experiment with robotics, build prototypes and learn by solving real problems.</p>
    <div class="callout"><strong>Working principles</strong><br/>Read carefully. Think independently. Write clearly. Build things. Test assumptions. Share what I learn.</div>
    <p class="small-note">This page describes interests and ambitions, not a claim of expertise in every field listed.</p>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>